{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1218366-a-few-questions-about-balance","id":1218366,"title":"A few questions about balance","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-13T17:18:19-07:00","id":1218366,"title":"A few questions about balance","content":"I am mostly familiar with CofD. How do the splats in classic WoD compare with each other balance wise? Can you be two supernaturals at the same time? How does Disciplines and Thaumaturgy fare against Sphere magick, Gifts and Changelings?<br /> <br /> <br /> (Frankly, I am more than a bit intimidated by the massive word count in the 20th Anniversary books. Mage in particular is giving me nightmarish eye strain.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23821,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23821-rathford","user":"Rathford","date":". 05-13-2018, 08:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23821-rathford","name":"Rathford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23821_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T17:50:44-07:00","id":1218375,"title":"","content":"They don't really compare. Cross-splat balance has always been a big headache for a fair number of ST. Some are more or less on par so It's doable. Any specific splat in mind? It might be easier to provide accurate feedback if we knew which one you were considering combining.<br /> <br /> No, you cannot be two (or more) supernatural at the same time (with the exception of the Abomination, but that never ends well). So no Vampiric Changeling for example.<br /> <br /> On one hand, Magick can be more powerful, depending on your Sphere and their rating, but you always have to worry about Paradox. Thaumaturgy and othr Blood-Magic is more static, but Paradox is not an issues and there are a great variaty of Paths and Ritual to learn, making it a bit easier to work. Changeling, not too sure (been too long since I've read it). Gifts are handy and quite useful, but are outclass for the most part, but that's not the Garou main strength either, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T18:02:40-07:00","id":1218378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boneguard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1218366-a-few-questions-about-balance?p=1218375#post1218375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any specific splat in mind? It might be easier to provide accurate feedback if we knew which one you were considering combining.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bVampire and Mage mostly. I am currently eyeing Changeling.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23821-rathford","name":"Rathford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23821_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T21:21:09-07:00","id":1218399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boneguard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1218366-a-few-questions-about-balance?p=1218375#post1218375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, you cannot be two (or more) supernatural at the same time (with the exception of the Abomination, but that never ends well). So no Vampiric Changeling for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Kiasyd come kinda close to being vampiric changelings. Not exactly, of course, but same wheelhouse... and a lot less destructive than abominations.<br /> <br /> Totally agree about everything else.<br /> <br /> Mages, in my experience, play poorly with just about every other supernatural. Sphere magic is nuts and postmodernism needs a nerf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T07:38:59-07:00","id":1218532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1218366-a-few-questions-about-balance?p=1218399#post1218399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Kiasyd come kinda close to being vampiric changelings. Not exactly, of course, but same wheelhouse... and a lot less destructive than abominations.<br /> <br /> Totally agree about everything else.<br /> <br /> Mages, in my experience, play poorly with just about every other supernatural. Sphere magic is nuts and postmodernism needs a nerf.</div> </div> </div> </div>We crossed over mage with a lot stuff, and sphere magick was kept on a leesh through paradox, and a strict use of paradigm and foci. These things really put mages in their place and keeps even pure mage stuff from turning into flavorless super powers.<br /> <br /> Add: there's also counter magick rules for other supernatural creatures in M20, Mage and Werewolf's Revised Storyteller's Handbook, Vampire 20, and some really old stuff in werewolf 2nd edition core and Chaos Factor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":21481,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","user":"Onkwe","date":". 05-22-2018, 04:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T08:51:05-07:00","id":1218566,"title":"","content":"In general all splats are crossover-able. Changelings got a big power up in 20th edition and wraith will probably, too. The three main splats, namely Vampires, Werwolfes and Mages are all on par, with each having a distinctive specialty (Vampire: politics, Werewolfs: direct combat, Mages: kicking your ass without you even knowing what's going on).<br /> <br /> Multi-Splatting is a very bad idea, as it totally disrupts balancing. That's why in every book there's the same mention: Vampirism is (mostly) incompatible with werewolfs, destroys the Avatar of Mages and snuffs out a Changelings fey-soul. And so on. I'm GMing a campaign at the moment with just a single player and we're experimenting a bit with heavy crossover and a bit of multi-splat characters (with some house rules, as they are heavily needed in this scenario). It's nothing I would ever consider in a game with more players. The balance get's thrown out of the window, even when a Mage is somehow allowed to soak lethal damage without having to cast a vulgar spell or be really, really well prepared. Same goes for most other combinations.<br /> <br /> Vampire and Mage is actually a really good crossover possibility. Aside from the virtues, which are not present in Mage rules, there are a lot of possibilities for Mages and Vampires to work together or against one another. There's a lot of shared history with the Tremere and the Order of Hermes, but also with the Tel'Mahe'Ra and the Euthanatos Mages. I'd suggest taking a look at all splats, just to make the cast of enemies (especially for combat) more diverse. Just because there are werewolves in your game doesn't mean Werewolf-lore has to be true. It doesn't even need to be mentioned at all. But having a really tough and well designed beast as an enemy can be very awesome.<br /> The obvious drawback is that there's a lot of systems coming together (Vampire-Disciplines, Werewolf-Gifts, Mage-Spheres and possibly Changeling Arts and Realms, Demon Lores, etc.), each of them working differently. Some have special stats (Arete, Gnosis, Faith, Glamour), others use Attribute+Ability dice pools.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T17:19:53-07:00","id":1218739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheVarulfen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1218366-a-few-questions-about-balance?p=1218566#post1218566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In general all splats are crossover-able. Changelings got a big power up in 20th edition and wraith will probably, too. The three main splats, namely Vampires, Werwolfes and Mages are all on par, with each having a distinctive specialty (Vampire: politics, Werewolfs: direct combat, Mages: kicking your ass without you even knowing what's going on).<br /> <br /> The obvious drawback is that there's a lot of systems coming together (Vampire-Disciplines, Werewolf-Gifts, Mage-Spheres and possibly Changeling Arts and Realms, Demon Lores, etc.), each of them working differently. Some have special stats (Arete, Gnosis, Faith, Glamour), others use Attribute+Ability dice pools.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a few people have pointed out, when it comes to crossing vampire (Ghouls) and Mages; Every experience point that you put into disciplines is an experience point that isn't going in to arete or your spheres. And even with Paradox-free disciplines, you're probably losing out compared to someone that puts the XP purely into the mage realms","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T19:27:15-07:00","id":1218772,"title":"","content":"Don't worry about balance. It's not what these systems are designed for. If that's a legitimate concern you shouldn't play crossover games using the classics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","name":"PazuzuAxelf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T12:03:41-07:00","id":1218990,"title":"","content":"The best way is to balance characters between each other (which is wise anyway even in 1 splat as options are not always well balanced), but the splat themselves... good luck with the headache.<br /> <br /> Although be mindful of some mechanics that can make the mix unpractical (Vampire sleeping at night, Changeling Mist, Werewolves Delirium etc)<br /> <br /> Mixing supernatural templates on one character doesn't really work, although (I believe) anyone (but Vampires) can be a ghoul though there are secondary effects. Alternatively, Vampire have theKiasyd/Maeghar for Changeling, the Tremere are ex Mages, Spiritus frm the Arhiman could be used to create a bloodline similar to the Kiasyd but coming from Kinfolks, Necromancers can cover Wraith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5462-kendaan","name":"Kendaan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T15:53:59-07:00","id":1219091,"title":"","content":"Something to keep in mind is that the splats are generally unbalanced, but their balance shifts depending on the situation. Put a vampire, a werewolf, and a mage in a white room fight, and the mage is going to suffer. So will the vampire, granted, because werewolves are combat monsters. But the mages suffer most, because they generally need a couple turns of using their Instruments, in order to get even essential Effects online. Like the kind of sensory Effects. Or the ability to soak anything but Bashing. Werewolves and vampires both innately soak at least lethal (and aggravated, if the vampire has Fortitude), whereas mages are squishy as any mortal, unless they can activate magick.<br /> <br /> All of that before Paradox is taken into consideration, which tends to hamstring mages in ways the other splats don't have to deal with.<br /> <br /> ON THE OTHER HAND, if we're talking about a situation where the mage has time to plan and prepare, they can fly circles around the other splats. Any number of sensory effects - up to and including far-sight and precognition - allow mages to know about the presence of other splats long before said splats would realize the mage is a threat (after all, mages &quot;read&quot; as humans to aura sense and the like). Give the mage time to perform Rituals, and they can be quite potent, in ways that only a blood magician doing similar levels of preparation can attempt to match. Mages are also incredibly versatile; Spheres are more freeform that Gifts, Disciplines, etc. While other splats usually do specific tricks very well and at the drop of a hat, a mage can weave highly specific and esoteric effects that few would even consider an option, almost as quickly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T10:41:29-07:00","id":1219308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illithid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1218366-a-few-questions-about-balance?p=1218739#post1218739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As a few people have pointed out, when it comes to crossing vampire (Ghouls) and Mages; Every experience point that you put into disciplines is an experience point that isn't going in to arete or your spheres. And even with Paradox-free disciplines, you're probably losing out compared to someone that puts the XP purely into the mage realms</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Might be true. But only after a lot of investments, as Spheres and Arete scale much slower than Attributes and Abilities (and you will need those, too). Also, there is much to gain from Disciplines, Lores, Arts and whatever the power of a splat is called.<br /> <br /> The reason why Balancing is not that great a problem is that you have a real, human Storyteller. Every good ST can make decisions on the fly to keep the game balanced even though a Mage, a Werewolf and a Vampire walk into a bar. Even when multi-splatting this is still possible until a certain point (though still, I wouldn't recommend it).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T15:41:01-07:00","id":1220975,"title":"","content":"If you want Mage vs. Vampire crossover rules, M20 goes into the most detail on this. It gives Vampires a counter-magick roll for effects directly targeted at them (Wits + Occult, or your Willpower, whichever is lower, against a difficulty of 7) and it lets Mages counter effects which relate to the Spheres.<br /> <br /> For example, a Mage rolls their Arete to set a Vampire on fire. They get 3 successes. The Vampire rolls the lower of their Wits + Occult or Willpower, which is 7, at Difficulty 7. They get 2 successes. Now the Forces effect has 1 success.<br /> <br /> This counter-magick must be DELIBERATE and conscious... a Vampire with 0 occult can't make the roll at all (you can't attempt a Knowledge roll without having at least 1 dot in it). If they can make the roll, they must have some idea of what's going on... they could roll to resist when they feel like this strange mortal is somehow controlling their emotions, or when this wizard-looking fellow conjures up a ball of flame, but they have to know they're being targeted in some sense. However if they do make the roll, they have the advantage. Wits + Occult, Difficulty 7, will overcome most impressive Sphere effects unless the Mage has reduced the Difficulty significantly or has a tonne of Arete.<br /> <br /> The Vampire tries to use Dominate to force the Mage to surrender. They roll Manipulation + Intimidation, against a difficulty of 7 (the Mage's Willpower), and they get 2 successes. However if the Mage has the Mind Sphere, then they may reflexively roll their Arete to soak the successes, at difficulty 7. They could get 2 successes (with luck!), and cancel the effect.<br /> <br /> As a niche little *, a Mage with an Arete of 8 or higher is harder to counterspell. Not only do they have a tonne of Arete for the dicepool, the countermagick of Kindred (and other supernaturals) is then raised in difficulty to match their Arete. This means that an exceptionally powerful Mage will destroy almost any Vampire in a direct mystical confrontation (but these are incredibly rare Mages).<br /> <br /> Lastly, if you want to use the Mind Sphere on a supernatural creature, the difficulty is often higher, especially if they possess a power of mental manipulation such as Dominate. A Mage trying to use Mind to control an Elder Vampire with Dominate might be rolling against their Willpower + 5. M20 explains all of this in detail if you need all of the specifics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 05-21-2018, 06:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T17:12:17-07:00","id":1221000,"title":"","content":"While Mage does seem to refer to Vampire disciplines in a way that leaves the disciplines as-is; every splat tends to describe their antagonists in the same &quot;Paradigm&quot; of rules.<br /> In Vampire books, it describes werewolves, changelings, wraiths and mages to have effective &quot;Disciplines&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-26T01:15:43-07:00","id":1222185,"title":"","content":"Outside of balance issues, something to also keep in mind is that different lines also have other issues of fairness and playability that Ive seen come up, if you and the table are aware of and help mitigate can work well.<br /> <br /> For instance, morality is a big part of Vampire and in a different way Wraith, but does not really have an equivalent in Werewolf or Mage. A Garou can wantonly slaughter a city block, but a Cainite (on Humanity) is going to quickly become unplayable. <br /> <br /> This sort of punishes them unfairly as they have to spend XP on Virtues/Humanity when no one else does, as they focus on different styles and themes. There are Paths, but that might not be what a player wants from playing a Vampire, (or might cause other incompatibility issues). Maybe be more lenient with loosing Humanity than you might be in a typical VtM game?<br /> <br /> Another thing to keep in mind is that WoD games are not really designed to be all that balanced even within their own line. Some options are just better overall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}